@startuml
title Customer-facing view navigation map (proposed)
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false

state "VIEW-C-001\nTravel portal home" as C001
state "VIEW-C-009\nSearch results" as C009
state "VIEW-C-010\nTravel detail" as C010
state "VIEW-C-011/C-012\nSign in or register" as C011 #E8F4FF
state "VIEW-C-014\nTraveller selection" as C014
state "VIEW-C-013\nMy travel" as C013
state "VIEW-C-004\nMy orders" as C004
state "VIEW-C-005\nPayment" as C005
state "VIEW-C-006\nTravel documents" as C006
state "VIEW-C-007\nTravel assistance" as C007
state "VIEW-C-008\nCustomer account" as C008

[*] --> C001 : enter customer interaction
C001 --> C009 : search with criteria
C009 --> C009 : revise criteria / no matches
C009 --> C010 : view product
C010 --> C009 : return to results
C009 --> C014 : add dated stock [authenticated]
C010 --> C014 : add confirmed stock [authenticated]
C009 --> C011 : add dated stock [not authenticated]
C010 --> C011 : add confirmed stock [not authenticated]
C011 --> C014 : identity resolved / resume pending add
C014 --> C013 : assign traveller / add position
C013 --> C009 : continue shopping
C013 --> C013 : remove position / placement conflict
C013 --> C004 : place order [all stock available]
C001 --> C011 : sign in
C001 --> C007 : request ongoing help
C004 --> C005 : make payment
C004 --> C006 : obtain eligible documents
C004 --> C007 : request assistance
C008 --> C004 : open My orders
C004 --> C001 : return to discovery

note bottom
  VIEW-C-002 Trip composition and VIEW-C-003 Sales offer are retired.
  The pre-order Travel is session-scoped; order placement is atomic.
  Availability conflict never creates a partial order.
end note
@enduml
